## 9. What If Changes Were Made Manually?

If you edit code yourself, or another developer changes files, the Second Brain will not automatically update simply because those files changed.

Open Claude Code or Codex in the repository and use:

> Review the current Git changes and compare them with the appropriate baseline.
>
> Identify meaningful frontend, backend, database, and workflow changes.
>
> Update the affected Second Brain documentation and development journal.
>
> Preserve existing requirements, approvals, and historical records.
>
> Verify everything against the actual implementation.
>
> Do not modify application code during this documentation-review task.

The AI can inspect uncommitted changes and committed Git history that are available locally.

