## 11. Important Limitations

### AI does not continuously monitor changes

A new VS Code window does not independently trigger documentation updates.

Claude Code and Codex can follow their project instructions while actively completing tasks, but manual code edits, remote commits, and direct database changes require an additional review or automation process.

### Instruction files do not guarantee perfect documentation

AI can misunderstand a change or overlook a dependency.

Review documentation updates, especially those involving business rules, authentication, payments, data integrity, or database relationships.

### Faster searching is not guaranteed

`PROJECT_INDEX.md` can reduce unnecessary exploration, but reading instruction files also consumes tokens.

Actual performance depends on the task, context, code complexity, and how efficiently the assistant searches.

### Obsidian is not a deployment system

Obsidian stores and displays project knowledge. It does not replace Git, source control, automated tests, database backups, or deployment procedures.

### Documentation must not expose internal information publicly

Keep `.project-memory`, `.obsidian`, internal documentation, development instructions, test fixtures, and secrets outside the publicly accessible production web root.

A `.gitignore` entry does not make files inaccessible through a web server.

